<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:s="https://wvusports.com/services/xml_schema/story" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title /><link>https://wvusports.com/rss/</link><description /><atom:link href="https://wvusports.com/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><language>en-us</language><ttl>60</ttl><item><title>Mountaineers Fall in Double Overtime to Washington in NCAA Second Round</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/mens-soccer-mountaineers-fall-in-double-overtime-to-washington-in-ncaa-second-round</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/mens-soccer-mountaineers-fall-in-double-overtime-to-washington-in-ncaa-second-round</guid><category>Men's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Men's Soccer Huddle pregame against Washington" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/22/MSOC_WVUvsWashington_Nov22_2026_TT-1.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 4-seed West Virginia University men's soccer team fell to No. 5-seed Washington, 1-0, in double-overtime, Sunday afternoon at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium. The Mountaineers end their season with a record of 13-3-4 while the Huskies improve to 12-4-5 and advance to the third round to play No. 1-seed Indiana.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/MSOC_WVUvsWashington_Nov22_2026_TT-1.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/MSOC_WVUvsWashington_Nov22_2026_TT-1.jpg"><media:title>Men's Soccer Huddle pregame against Washington</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/MSOC_WVUvsWashington_Nov22_2026_TT-1.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:32:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>6</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59747</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Fall at Kansas State in Four Sets</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/volleyball-mountaineers-fall-at-kansas-state-in-four-sets</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/volleyball-mountaineers-fall-at-kansas-state-in-four-sets</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="West Virginia volleyball huddles after a point while playing against Kansas State" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/22/DTB04257.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. - The West Virginia University volleyball team (13-13, 6-10 Big 12) dropped a four-set match to Kansas State on Sunday afternoon at Morgan Family Arena in Manhattan, Kansas. The Mountaineers fell by set scores of 25-21, 21-25, 30-28 and 25-18.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/DTB04257.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/DTB04257.jpg"><media:title>West Virginia volleyball huddles after a point while playing against Kansas State</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/DTB04257.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:40:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59746</s:story_id></item><item><title>No. 23 West Virginia Defeats American</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/wrestling-no-23-west-virginia-defeats-american</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/wrestling-no-23-west-virginia-defeats-american</guid><category>Wrestling</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Luke Satriano competes against a wrestler for American at Hope Coliseum on Nov. 22, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Wrestling_vAmerican_11222026-2nd-2.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 23 West Virginia University wrestling team defeated American, 28-6, at Hope Coliseum in Morgantown on Sunday.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Wrestling_vAmerican_11222026-2nd-2.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Wrestling_vAmerican_11222026-2nd-2.jpg"><media:title>Luke Satriano competes against a wrestler for American at Hope Coliseum on Nov. 22, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Wrestling_vAmerican_11222026-2nd-2.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:32:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>18</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59745</s:story_id></item><item><title>West Tower Construction At Milan Puskar Stadium Will Halt Vehicular and Pedestrian Traffic</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/general-west-tower-construction-at-milan-puskar-stadium-will-halt-vehicular-and-pedestrian-traffic</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/general-west-tower-construction-at-milan-puskar-stadium-will-halt-vehicular-and-pedestrian-traffic</guid><category>Football, General</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Construction of the new West Tower at Milan Puskar Stadium will impact traffic and walking areas for the next two years." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Stadium_Map__11-20_-transparent.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – With the completion of the 2026 home football schedule, demolition of the 46-year old press box at Milan Puskar Stadium will commence on Monday, Nov. 23.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Stadium_Map__11-20_-transparent.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Stadium_Map__11-20_-transparent.jpg"><media:title>Construction of the new West Tower at Milan Puskar Stadium will impact traffic and walking areas for the next two years.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Stadium_Map__11-20_-transparent.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>3</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59744</s:story_id></item><item><title>Houston Kicks Late Field Goal to Down West Virginia</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/21/football-houston-kicks-late-field-goal-to-down-west-virginia</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/21/football-houston-kicks-late-field-goal-to-down-west-virginia</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="John Neider secures a 3-yard Michael Hawkins Jr. pass for a touchdown in the first quarter of West Virginia's game against 20th-ranked Houston at Milan Puskar Stadium." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/21/Neider-Main.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Jonathan Dimas' 23-yard field goal with four seconds left lifted 20th-ranked Houston to a 34-31 victory over West Virginia today at Milan Puskar Stadium.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/21/Neider-Main.jpg" /><medi